20,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
21,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
22,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
23,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems complaints about leaning bikes are common but ignored. Also, charging fees in other buildings can cause social friction and arrears.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Yumi,,The same people have had the best spots for years without any review! But daily riders say they'd actually prefer paying for a spot.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"It's a mess. People are shifting other bikes to get out, and some spots are completely exposed to rain. It's not a fair layout.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Our account is nearly empty, so we can't afford upgrades. Meanwhile, the ward park is expensive and has a long waiting list.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Adding billing would increase the treasurer's workload significantly. Also, those double-tier racks are physically demanding and require regular maintenance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, if daily riders are willing to pay, maybe that solves the fairness issue without causing the friction I feared.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"Exactly! It feels like the current ""silent"" arrangement is what's actually making people grumpy.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, if the racks are a pain to use and maintain, we should probably avoid them regardless of the space they save.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, the ward park is too full to be a viable alternative for everyone. We have to solve this internally.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,I agree with Ryuji. The physical effort and the paperwork for a paid system are both burdens we must consider.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we go with a lottery, it's fair, but does it solve the ""leaning bike"" problem Ryuji mentioned?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"Maybe not, but it stops the feeling that some people are ""special"" and keep the best spots forever.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,A lottery doesn't change the fact that some spots are wet and others are blocked. The physical chaos remains.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A paid system creates a fund for the building, which we desperately need since the ledger is so bare.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Toshio,,But who manages the money? The treasurer is already spending hours on small collections.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We need to balance financial gain, administrative ease, and social harmony.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I just want everyone to feel it's fair.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I want a system where I don't have to move someone else's bike at 8 AM.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Rationality suggests we monetize the demand if the ward park is full and we are broke.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I prefer the option with the least amount of ongoing monthly administration.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
46,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
47,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
48,3,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
49,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A brings money but risks arrears and tension. Option B is fair but random. Option C is efficient but physically difficult.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I like Option A because the daily riders said they'd prefer it, and it ends the ""same people"" problem.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is out because of the maintenance and difficulty. Between A and B, B is simpler for the residents.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is the only one that addresses our empty building account. It's the most rational choice.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the most sustainable. No monthly billing, no complex maintenance, just one draw a year.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, a lottery is clean. It avoids the ""debtor"" tension I saw in the neighboring block's report.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Yumi,,But @Shunichi is right about the money. Could we do a lottery with a small fee?,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,That just makes it Option A with extra steps. Let's keep it simple. I vote for the lottery.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, the ""fairness"" of a lottery is an illusion if the best spots are still randomly assigned to people who don't use them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Toshio,,The administrative burden of Option A is too high for our current volunteer structure.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I'm leaning toward Option B. It's the safest for the building's social atmosphere.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"I'm torn, but if the others hate the paperwork, maybe the lottery is better.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It's the most objective way to handle limited space.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I still maintain that Paid Allocation is the only way to actually improve the facility over time.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Toshio,,Simplicity wins. I'm voting for the lottery.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Let's vote.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"Okay, I'll go with the lottery to keep the peace.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll stick to my guns.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Toshio,,Ready.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
